{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromyTower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromyTower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.monodromy_powTrace_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.monodromy_powTrace_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromyTower.lean#L70-L75","doc":"**The carried monodromy's trace tower (from the class).** Any `BringWPlaneMonodromy` instance's\noperator generates the depth-2 SL₂ trace tower `t_{n+2} = (tr M)·t_{n+1} − t_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.powTrace_seeds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.powTrace_seeds","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromyTower.lean#L60-L68","doc":"The first two rungs of the tower are the universal SL₂ trace seeds: `t₀ = tr(I) = 2` and\n`t₁ = tr M`. With `powTrace_recurrence` these determine the whole tower `t_n = tr(Mⁿ)` — the depth-2\nrigidity: two seeds fix every higher rung (so a depth-2 SL₂ tower has only two free parameters, the\nformalized sense in which fitting the low-`n` `lw` values over-determines it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.powTrace_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.powTrace_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromyTower.lean#L51-L58","doc":"**The depth-2 SL₂ power-trace tower recurrence.** The trace tower `t_n := tr(Mⁿ)` of a unimodular\n2×2 monodromy satisfies the Chebyshev / Lucas depth-2 *linear* recurrence\n`t_{n+2} = (tr M)·t_{n+1} − t_n`, with `τ = tr M`. (Linear ⇒ `t_n = O((tr-dominant-root)ⁿ)`,\nexponential — the structural reason the depth-2 SL₂ fit is only `n ≤ 4` effective vs the\nsuper-exponential `a_D^(n) = lw(n−1)`; sibling z2bn, #2795/#2800/#2808.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.unimodular_pow_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.unimodular_pow_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromyTower.lean#L41-L49","doc":"**The matrix-power recurrence.** From `M² = (tr M)·M − I` (`unimodular_two_recurrence`), every\npower of a unimodular 2×2 monodromy obeys the same depth-2 recurrence:\n`M^{n+2} = (tr M)·M^{n+1} − Mⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}